# Review: RecorderPlugin

The plugin implements the whole spec. `TakeRecorder` opens the inputs in the click, counts in 3-2-1 and
runs one `MediaRecorder` per slide. `saveTake` appends a new Variant and makes it main. The overlay,
both Recordings companions, the settings and the three take operations (with a DeleteTake/RestoreTake
undo mapping) are all wired to their surfaces. What is tested is the pure core: device choice and
processing-off constraints, the level-meter state, per-slide segmenting, WAV concatenation and take
naming. Nothing tests the recorder class, the take operations, the companions or the overlay, and no
e2e exercises a recording, so most requirements are `untested`. There are no divergences.

Of 25 items: 7 done, 17 untested, 0 partial, 0 diverged, 1 missing (QA-1, a human-only test).

